0010: module M5d instrumentation (ViGraph / ViGraphEstimator mutation log), active only with OKVIS_PORT_GRAPH_DUMP_DIR.
 New header okvis_ceres/include/okvis/ceres/OkvisPortVigraphLog.hpp: every OUTERMOST ViGraph / ViGraphEstimator
 mutation (nested calls such as removeObservation inside convertToPoseGraphMst are not logged) and every direct access
 of ViSlamBackend to a graph (initial fixation, constant/variable landmarks, observation information, copying states into
 the full graph, ImuError::syncFrom, landmark classification) is written as a framed record (tag >= 32; layouts in
 okvis_port/c/ok_vigraph.h) into the same problem.bin stream as the Ceres Problem log of patch 0009, right AFTER the
 Problem calls it made (one RAII scope per mutation, written on exit). ViGraph::optimise() additionally logs the graph
 state before the solve (states, the digest of every parameter block incl. landmark quality / classification, the digest
 of every IMU term) and what the solver changed afterwards (parameter values, IMU re-integration state), so a replay can
 compare the whole graph at every optimise() and carry the solver output into its own state. ImuError gets a read-only
 accessor of its redo state. Observational only: no computed value changes, no uninitialised memory is read.
